      "created_at": "2026-02-09T07:24:56Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-02-09T07:29:21Z",
      "body_html": "<p dir=\"auto\">The question is the design of <code class=\"notranslate\">Node::new</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">TreeNodeValue::rel_children</code> makes <code class=\"notranslate\">Node::default(lv).rel_children(None)</code> a compulsory requirement to prove <code class=\"notranslate\">new_preserves_inv</code>. I've thought about decomposing the properties into several traits, but this is not an easy one, because <code class=\"notranslate\">TreeNodeValue::default()</code> requires a <code class=\"notranslate\">nat</code> argument. So modifications of these are good.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">But I don't like the modification in <code class=\"notranslate\">recursive_insert</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">recursive_remove</code>. They should just insert or remove, and I don't think we should check <code class=\"notranslate\">rel_children</code> in this function. Instead, we may need another function to check whether the <code class=\"notranslate\">inserted/removed</code> node satisfies <code class=\"notranslate\">rel_children</code> and add it to the preconditions of <code class=\"notranslate\">insert/remove_preserves_inv</code>. I've removed the change in these two functions.</p>",
      "body_text": "The question is the design of Node::new and TreeNodeValue::rel_children makes Node::default(lv).rel_children(None) a compulsory requirement to prove new_preserves_inv. I've thought about decomposing the properties into several traits, but this is not an easy one, because TreeNodeValue::default() requires a nat argument. So modifications of these are good.\nBut I don't like the modification in recursive_insert and recursive_remove. They should just insert or remove, and I don't think we should check rel_children in this function. Instead, we may need another function to check whether the inserted/removed node satisfies rel_children and add it to the preconditions of insert/remove_preserves_inv. I've removed the change in these two functions.",
      "body": "The question is the design of `Node::new` and `TreeNodeValue::rel_children` makes `Node::default(lv).rel_children(None)` a compulsory requirement to prove `new_preserves_inv`. I've thought about decomposing the properties into several traits, but this is not an easy one, because `TreeNodeValue::default()` requires a `nat` argument. So modifications of these are good.\r\n\r\nBut I don't like the modification in `recursive_insert` and `recursive_remove`. They should just insert or remove, and I don't think we should check `rel_children` in this function. Instead, we may need another function to check whether the `inserted/removed` node satisfies `rel_children` and add it to the preconditions of `insert/remove_preserves_inv`. I've removed the change in these two functions.\r\n \r\n",
      "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
